# Line-ending policy, so a checkout on any OS round-trips byte-identically.
#
# # Why .bat and .cmd MUST be CRLF
#
# `cmd.exe` parses a batch file line by line and a LONE LF breaks it: the whole
# file is read as one line. `tools/check_batch_encoding.py` enforces "pure ASCII +
# CRLF" for exactly that reason, and it failed intermittently when a checkout on
# Linux wrote LF endings into `Run.bat` - the diff then showed every line as
# changed while the content was identical.
#
# 行尾策略，使任何操作系统上的检出都能逐字节往返。
#
# # 为什么 .bat 与 .cmd 必须是 CRLF
#
# `cmd.exe` 逐行解析批处理文件，而"单独的" LF 会让它失效：整个文件被当成一行读取。
# `tools/check_batch_encoding.py` 正是因此强制"纯 ASCII + CRLF"，而当 Linux 上的检出把 LF
# 写进 `Run.bat` 时它会间歇性失败——此时 diff 会显示每一行都变了，而内容完全相同。

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary artefacts must never be normalised.
# 二进制产物绝不能做行尾规范化。
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.pdb binary
